WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.769
He's one of Hollywood's biggest stars today,
but the road to success wasn't exactly smooth

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:07.330
for Ryan Reynolds.

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:12.170
He's the first to admit that there's been,
quote, "nothing meteoric" about his career,

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:16.180
which has progressed slowly since he left
Vancouver for Los Angeles.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.890
From his early struggles growing up, to making
movies that even he never watched, this is

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:25.480
how Ryan Reynolds went from college dropout
to becoming Deadpool.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.060
Honing his skills

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:32.090
Reynolds' father, Jim, was a former boxer
and policeman who passed away in 2015.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:35.690
And according to Ryan, he wasn't an easy man
to live with.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:36.899
Reynolds told GQ,

00:00:36.899 --> 00:00:40.010
"Sometimes it felt a little like a military
barracks.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:45.620
You know, get the fold exactly right on the
bed, make sure there's no speck of lint anywhere."

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:50.429
The fear of disappointing his father turned
Reynolds into a self-proclaimed "really nervous

00:00:50.429 --> 00:00:54.859
kid," but it also helped him to develop skills
that would serve him well later in life.

00:00:54.859 --> 00:00:55.859
He told the mag,

00:00:55.859 --> 00:00:59.819
"I was extremely sensitive [and] incredibly
perceptive.

00:00:59.819 --> 00:01:03.690
[...] It was so acute that I really was able
to jump into other people's skin."

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.480
45 minutes of college

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.250
As a teen, he landed a role on Nickelodeon's
Fifteen, but after high school, the acting

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.230
gigs dried up and Reynolds worked two jobs
to make ends meet.

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:20.250
He then enrolled in a college criminology
course, but he lasted less than an hour, telling

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:21.250
Variety,

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.530
"I'm not being facetious.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:27.490
I spent 45 minutes in college, and I turned
around and said, 'I'm going to drive to L.A.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:29.350
and try to get into the Groundlings.'"

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:33.680
Just before he made the move to California,
he landed a role on The X-Files, though it

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.500
did little for his confidence.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:40.050
"We gotta kick some butt.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.320
Like I'm sure Bruno's doing in heaven right
now."

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.350
Spoiler alert: it wasn't much of a role.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:49.420
Still, Reynolds claims he got bad advice from
director Rob Bowman, saying,

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:53.439
"He told me never to go to Hollywood because
I'd never make it there.

00:01:53.439 --> 00:01:58.070
[...] And secondly, that I could have a very
small yet profitable career here in Vancouver

00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:59.450
doing small parts."

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:04.310
But Bowman's discouraging words only made
Reynolds all the more determined to go for

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:05.310
it.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.950
Two Guys, a Girl and a breakout star

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:12.980
Reynolds' really big break came when he won
his role on ABC's Two Guys, a Girl and a Pizza

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.349
Place in 1998.

00:02:14.349 --> 00:02:18.299
"The valve at the end of the colon that regulates
discharge.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.680
Is, uh...the poopie chute."

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:28.300
In 2016, he told Andy Cohen that he'd sign
up for a reunion "in a heartbeat" because

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.529
he had so much fun making the show, which
he credits with giving him the confidence

00:02:32.529 --> 00:02:34.370
to make it as a movie star.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:40.879
"That sitcom is, I know it's more en vogue
to say that film is where it's at, and it's

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:43.499
great, but that job was so much fun for me."

00:02:43.499 --> 00:02:48.370
Renamed after two seasons, Two Guys and a
Girl aired for four years, providing Reynolds

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:53.790
with a steady income and lots of experience,
which he would take to the big screen.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:54.790
Party guy

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:59.890
After Two Guys and a Girl wrapped, Reynolds
took on the title role in college romp National

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:01.769
Lampoon's Van Wilder.

00:03:01.769 --> 00:03:04.889
The film was hammered by critics but became
a cult favorite.

00:03:04.889 --> 00:03:08.209
"I'm doing a human interest piece... on you."

00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:09.409
"Well, I'm flattered.

00:03:09.409 --> 00:03:11.230
I'd love for your piece to be on me."

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:16.129
Van Wilder put Reynolds on the map and led
to numerous offers, but he told GQ,

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:19.379
"For years after that, I was Van Wilder.

00:03:19.379 --> 00:03:21.139
It made me the party guy.

00:03:21.139 --> 00:03:24.519
I would walk into a bar and people would start
lining up the shots.

00:03:24.519 --> 00:03:28.559
You could sum up my career at that point as
a free shot at a bar."

00:03:28.559 --> 00:03:29.889
Overcoming anxiety

00:03:29.889 --> 00:03:35.569
In 2018, Reynolds revealed to The New York
Times that the anxiety he experienced as a

00:03:35.569 --> 00:03:37.790
child still plagues him today.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:42.010
With two Deadpool movies under his belt and
an X-Force feature on the way, he's at the

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.499
top of his game, but told the Times,

00:03:44.499 --> 00:03:46.370
"I've always had anxiety.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.349
Both in the lighthearted, 'I'm anxious about
this' kind of thing, and I've been to the

00:03:50.349 --> 00:03:53.669
depths of the darker end of the spectrum,
which is not fun."

00:03:53.669 --> 00:03:57.239
"What if I told you we can cure you, and give
you abilities?"

00:03:57.239 --> 00:03:59.499
"I'd say that you sound like an infomercial.

00:03:59.499 --> 00:04:01.650
But not a good one."

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:06.519
After years of taking a "hard-knock" approach
to his problem, he decided he needed to change,

00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:07.519
saying,

00:04:07.519 --> 00:04:12.599
"I realized it was time to just effectively
light a match to my life and walk away.

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:14.719
[...] It's the best thing I ever did."

00:04:14.719 --> 00:04:19.410
Today, he keeps his anxiety in check using
the Headspace meditation app.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.380
The Green Lantern curse

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:25.870
After his role in Blade:Trinity, Reynolds'
fortunes were hit-and-miss.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:30.790
He won acclaim for his work in The Nines,
Definitely Maybe and Buried, but bombed with

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:34.540
The Amityville Horror, Just Friends, and Smokin'
Aces.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:39.560
When Green Lantern came around in 2011, he
needed a hit, but didn't get it.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:43.500
He said in an interview with Variety,

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:44.560
"I represented the death of the superhero
for a while.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:48.600
So, you know, after Green Lantern, in that
category, I was pretty much unhirable."

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:53.530
Reynolds has mocked the movie on several occasions
in the years since, both on talk shows and

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:54.530
on social media.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:57.330
"If you could rate the Green Lantern on a
scale of 1-10."

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.330
"Four, maybe?"

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.330
"You'd give it a four?!"

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:00.330
"Three or four?"

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:02.020
"You'd give it a three or four?"

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.020
"It didn't work.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:04.020
One!

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.190
It's a one!"

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:09.360
And he didn't pull any punches when it came
to poking fun at Green Lantern as Deadpool,

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.360
either.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.390
"And please don't make the super suit green.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.640
Or animated."

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.240
Career-saving leak

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:20.900
He lobbied hard for a decade, but it wasn't
actually Reynolds that convinced Fox to move

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.560
forward with Deadpool — it was the fans.

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:28.590
The film got the green light after test footage
leaked online and social media users went

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.050
nuts.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.050
Reynolds told Variety,

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:36.500
"When the leaked footage got around the internet,
it created this enormous groundswell.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:42.670
I credit Twitter users, Facebook users, and
Instagram users for getting this movie made."

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:47.190
With the failure of Green Lantern still fresh
in their minds, Fox was hesitant to fund a

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:49.740
superhero movie fronted by Reynolds.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:50.740
He admitted,

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:55.390
"Part of the reason Deadpool wasn't greenlit
right away was certainly because of me.

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:59.860
If Robert Downey Jr. was playing it, I don't
know how much greener a light you can get

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:00.870
to make a movie."

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.060
So, who actually leaked the footage?

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:08.120
For the longest time Reynolds suspected that
director Tim Miller was behind it, but he's

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:12.140
now convinced that an unknown Fox employee
got the ball rolling.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.140
Reynolds told Yahoo!,

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:17.780
"The initial [leak] came from Fox, they think
— someone recorded the footage on their

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:19.690
iPhone and then released it.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:24.310
And then once that happened, somebody hacked
into Blur Studios and got the original footage

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:26.810
in high-res and put it online."

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:28.970
The rest, as they say, is history.

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:31.230
"Bring it on, One Eyed Willie."

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:32.360
Thanks for watching!

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:35.630
